"`model_v2.md` is saved. The mathematical formulation:\n\n**Decision variables**\n- xA = units of A produced per week (units/week)\n- xB = units of B produced per week (units/week)\n\n**Objective**\n- maximize Z = 40·xA + 50·xB [USD/week]\n\n**Constraints**\n- Machine: 2·xA + 1·xB ≤ 100 [hours/week]\n- Labor: 1·xA + 3·xB ≤ 90 [hours/week]\n- xA, xB ≥ 0 [units/week]\n\nA couple of things I added beyond the bare math:\n\n- **Unit checks on every equation** — so it's explicit that coefficients × variables actually cancel into the right units (e.g. h/unit × units/week = h/week).\n- **Standard matrix form** (max cᵀx s.t. Ax ≤ b, x ≥ 0) with the A matrix, c, and b vectors written out — handy if we solve it with a simplex implementation or a solver library.\n- **A traceability table** mapping each v1 statement to its v2 formalization, so the chain from words → math is auditable.\n\nNext natural step is solving it — want the optimal plan (and which constraint ends up binding)? 🦀"